What changed
New EXECUTION BOUNDARY section at the top — an explicit allowlist/denylist. Even curl against localhost is forbidden for the agent; even if the user says "run it," it must decline and re-print the command.
Agent-allowed commands narrowed to read-only file ops + lockfile-based scanners (npm audit --package-lock-only touches no app).
No "approval per batch" anymore — the old prompt allowed execution after user approval; that's removed entirely.
Workflow loop flipped: Codex generates → you execute → paste output → Codex interprets and updates finding status (UNVERIFIED → VERIFIED-CONFIRMED/DISMISSED).
Test Command Pack is now a first-class deliverable with setup exports, expected outputs for vulnerable vs. patched, and cleanup steps — designed for copy-paste, not for the agent to touch.
